secubox-toolbox (1.1.0-1~bookworm1) bookworm; urgency=medium

  * Add inject_banner mitmproxy addon: HTML response interception injects a
    visible MITM transparency banner with the CA SHA1 fingerprint. Allows
    inspected users to verify against their iPhone Settings\ Cert Trust.
    Idempotent (no double-inject), z-index max, closable.
  * Add /api/v1/toolbox/ca/fingerprint endpoint (SHA1+SHA256+subject).
  * Add /api/v1/toolbox/client-status endpoint : reports captive_subnet,
    r2_consented, validated flags + CA fingerprint + mac_hash. Used by
    JS clients to display in-context MITM status.
  * systemd unit: load inject_banner.py addon.
  * Closes #477.

 -- Gerald KERMA <devel@cybermind.fr>  Thu, 04 Jun 2026 08:05:00 +0200


secubox-toolbox (1.0.0-1~bookworm1) bookworm; urgency=medium

  * Initial release — Phase 1 du parent #474 "ToolBoX Pipeline".
  * Captive portal FastAPI : splash, consent R2, MAC hashing (sel rotatif),
    SQLite store events.
  * CA distribution : mobileconfig iOS (placeholder unsigned), DER pour Android,
    page d'aide install par-OS.
  * nftables transparent TPROXY template (validated_macs/consented_r2_macs/quarantine_macs).
  * mitmproxy addons squelettes : cookies, dpi, avatar, ja4, soc_relay → POST
    vers sockets existants (cookies.sock, dpi.sock, avatar.sock, threat-analyst.sock,
    soc.sock).
  * systemd : secubox-toolbox.service (FastAPI) + secubox-toolbox-mitm.service
    (mitmdump transparent).
  * Scripts : toolbox-up (compose nft), ca-init (gen CA self-signed 10y).
  * WebUI admin /toolbox/ + menu.d/26-toolbox.json (category=security).
  * Closes #475.

